Measured 21:58 on MInArmZA (Teach HOME): drive home, then the +200 back-off went DOWN, then golden
case 500's MoveAbs to ZSafePos=50 came back UP. EastSun first asked for "up 200 and stop" (a
-200 / no-ZSafePos version was built on o2, never committed), then to remove the back-off altogether.
This commit is the exact inverse of 71e7d7b (MachineType.h W906_Z_HOME_BACKOFF_PULSE, Motor/EcatMotorRoute.h
W906_IsZAxisAlias, TMyEtherCatMotor::iW906ZHomeBackoff + EtherCatMotHome Task 30, TMyMotor::Home,
WebMotorAccess TickHomes phase 2 + g_W906ZHomeBackoff, the test block). Z home = drive home ->
arm Z to ZSafePos (golden case 500) -> HomeFlag=1, as before 71e7d7b.

o2 clean rebuild (the touched files recompiled): wb_serve + test_web_motor_access + test_pci1203_motor_route;
ctest WebMotorAccess, Pci1203MotorRoute pass; "Z back-off" no longer in wb_serve.exe.
